# What's new card after an update (#158).
# Release keys are listed in data/whats-new.json, newest first.

whats-new-title = What's new in werdy
whats-new-version = Version { $version }
whats-new-close = Got it
whats-new-region = What changed since your last visit

## 0.3.0

whats-new-0-3-0-groups = Every deed now sits in one place: a time of day, or a group such as Quran or Dua. Deeds from the Academy level sets move into their groups once, by themselves.
whats-new-0-3-0-schedules = Two new schedules: once a week, and when it comes up.
whats-new-0-3-0-hours = Count goals can now be set in hours.
whats-new-0-3-0-prayers = The five prayers in Reports now show missed and unmarked days.
whats-new-0-3-0-support = The people you share your deeds with are now called Support: those who support you, and those you support.
whats-new-0-3-0-sheet = Smaller mark buttons, long text wraps onto a new line, and you can change the language in Settings.
whats-new-0-3-0-late = Starting werdy late in the week? You can also mark the past seven days.
whats-new-0-3-0-offline = werdy now opens without internet, and having it open in the browser and on the home screen at once no longer breaks sync.

## 0.2.0

whats-new-0-2-0-sheet = The daily sheet is tighter: one surface, a chip for each prayer time, times you can fold away, and counts you can type.
whats-new-0-2-0-open = Tap the open count to see only the deeds you have not marked yet.
whats-new-0-2-0-reminders = Prayer reminders on the web. Sign in, turn them on in Settings, and werdy reminds you after each adhan.
whats-new-0-2-0-watch = Ask someone to support your deeds, or ask to support theirs, with their Google email. They see your request when they sign in.
whats-new-0-2-0-reports = Reports now read at a glance: one headline, a bar for each day, your strongest and weakest deeds, and your prayers.
whats-new-0-2-0-levels = The three Academy level sheets are now ready sets you can add to your sheet.
